\item[\  \ suggested semantics:] dna
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\
Values for the attribute `synvps' for basic verbs
\item rules:\\
these transformations follow the startrules\\
In cases of doubt about the direct or indirect object status of the argument 
without a prep, the translation into other languages should decide (e.g.\ 
{\em strike\/}, which might seem to take a direct object/theme `strike sb', but which 
translates into `overkomen {\em op\/} iemand').
\end{enumerate}
